    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1205 by French crusaders, it was the most durable <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#latin">Latin</a> state created in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#greece">Greece</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>.</li><li>A model feudal society of twelve baronies, its customs were codified in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#assizes-of-romania">Assizes of Romania</a>.</li><li>Defeat at Pelagonia in 1259 cost it Mistras, the base from which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> reconquered the Peloponnese by 1432.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Venetian writer Marino Sanudo Torsello reported that at the princes’ court in the Peloponnese French was spoken as well as in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#paris">Paris</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

